soc: sprd: minidump: the kernel log into the Unisoc bootloader's sysdumpdb

A failed mainline boot on the U30 Pro leaves no log: the bootloader rolls the slot back with a power-off, so
RAM (ramoops) is gone before Android runs. After an abnormal reset (the PMIC watchdog) the bootloader saves
the sections of the minidump record in sysdump_info to the sysdumpdb partition first. Publish the printk
ring and a kmsg_dump text copy there, in the layout of Unisoc's sysdump driver.

